        "created_at": "2011-08-23T18:21:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Christopher&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Christopher\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I was just reading through the FallCon (an awesome con in Canada) blog, and ran across these pages.  Thought they might help!</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.fallcon.com/_blog/FallCon_Blog/post/How_to_Teach_Games_An_Introduction_(Part_1)/\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.fallcon.com/_blog/FallCon_Blog/post/How_to_Teach_Games_An_Introduction_(Part_1)/</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.fallcon.com/_blog/FallCon_Blog/post/How_to_Teach_Games_General_Tips_(Part_2)/\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.fallcon.com/_blog/FallCon_Blog/post/How_to_Teach_Games_General_Tips_(Part_2)/</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.fallcon.com/_blog/FallCon_Blog/post/How_to_Teach_Games_The_Framework_(Part_3)/\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.fallcon.com/_blog/FallCon_Blog/post/How_to_Teach_Games_The_Framework_(Part_3)/</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks, those links are a good resource. As a veteran demo representative they were enlightening. I am still looking for SotM specific demo ideas though.</p>",
