      {
        "id": 21817,
        "name": "Paul",
        "username": "Paul",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/{size}/5862_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-23T19:16:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think that it is most helpful in demos to keep the game moving.  I tend to show people an efficient way to lay out their play space (where to put the character card, the deck, in play cards, dice/hp counters, etc) so that they can see everything that is going on the first time they play.  I also quickly explain some of the key concepts of the game (what the card types are, how the turn works, etc).</p>\n<p>I think that those two things are key to a good, smooth gameplay experience.  We try to do both of those things in the rule book (with the gameplay layout diagram, and the quick rules), but I know that sometimes people tl;dr the rule book <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=9\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
